{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/292247-your-character-s-theme-songs","id":292247,"title":"Your Character's Theme Songs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T11:23:34-07:00","id":292247,"title":"Your Character's Theme Songs?","content":"I have to listen to certain music to get in one of my characters mind, to get how he moves, he talks and such? WHich bands do you hear to Tune Up with your characters?<br /> for Joe Torienark the Nuwisha: Roller coaster of love (red hot chilly pepper) all the Harmonica Music from Cowboy Bebop , Far Side of Crazy. and the Trigun Soundtack<br /> <br /> Crowley: Sympathy of the Devil and Rolling Stones in General, Morrisey / The Smiths<br /> <br /> Travis Connor: Irish Brujah, claims to be the The Fifth Sex Pistol but he was kicked out, Sex Pistols, The Clash<br /> <br /> David Blackthorn: Wraith .. Joy Division and The Cure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-25-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T14:57:35-07:00","id":292437,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">For Sabbat games, I'll listen to Eisbrecher (and some Megaherz). &quot;Mein Blut&quot; makes me think of a Pack about to go on a suicide mission (for some reason) and &quot;Supermodel&quot; makes me think of the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> For Wraith games - and I know this is going to sound weird - I like Johnny Cash. No idea why, but &quot;Ring of Fire&quot; just makes me think of Helldiving. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:51:54-07:00","id":292889,"title":"","content":"Ha. I saw this topic... and you know what I thought?<br /> <br /> That it is kinda sad there are a ton of great songs in languages other than English that are never translated to English and thus perpetually unknown by the general public. I, for example, am a big fan of Polish poetic singing (I don't know if that's actually a term in English but I mean songs that are basically made from things that could easily do as poetry without the music) but whenever I'd like to share some of it with people online they just wouldn't get it. They could enjoy the music, but let's be honest - in this kind of works words are equally as important. Or even more.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my character theme was a fragment of one such song.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://w28.wrzuta.pl/audio/30mUYDjKoEv/zbroja_-_jacek_kaczmarski_fragment\" target=\"_blank\">http://w28.wrzuta.pl/audio/30mUYDjKo...arski_fragment</a><br /> <br /> <br /> It translates roughly as follows (though I assure you - it loses most of it's charm. Actually all of it. As you are probably aware, translating poetry - especially the kind that rhymes - is a serious, serious bsns. And I couldn't even translate a book properly, let alone a song. But I personally chose this particular song because the message resonated well with my character).<br /> <br /> Lord, you gave my an armor, wrought by the smiths of old.<br /> Tested in many battles and baptised in blood.<br /> I trip with every step I take in this armor forged for a giant;<br /> because it stings my side like a conscience's blackmail.<br /> <br /> (Refrain)<br /> And though the helmet and the sword had been lost<br /> and it's no bulwark for the body anymore<br /> An armor such as this - it's still worth a life!<br /> <br /> Magical runes scribed upon it, now readable by none<br /> But it was forged from myths - and (is) eternal like a myth.<br /> It has trapped my body, hinders my sleep and my life<br /> and masses laugh at a dwarf, who wishes to play a giant. - (This line sort of perfectly describes my late character. Or maybe all of them. They are - as I am - often wide-eyed idealists, always in the pursue of some &quot;higher values&quot;.As you may guess, it regularly plays out shitty in real life. And even worse in WoD)<br /> <br /> (Ref.)<br /> <br /> And such is the dignity of the long dried-out blood<br /> That I feel how it demands me to grow<br /> Though it may be in vain, I will stand (in the aforementioned armor) for a hundred man<br /> But please Lord, relieve me of it, should I die in my sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Huh. Now I totally butchered the works of one of the best Polish modern poetic singers. I should be proud of myself. Basically, if you couldn't figure it out - and I wouldn't blame you (not only bacause of *cough* &quot;translation&quot; *cough*, but also because it's basically a cut-out fragment of the whole song) - the song is a one big metaphor. The &quot;armor&quot; is a baggage of traditions and customs widely believed to belong in the past now. Honor, sincerity even in the face of punishment, loyalty, defiance.<br /> <br /> Thus, the &quot;armor&quot; is basically useless. It offers no protection. Even worse - it makes life difficult for those who wear it. Even then, the subject proudly claims, that it's still &quot;worth a life&quot; to him, despite the fact that it was &quot;forged for a giant&quot; and he &quot;trips with every step&quot;, making the people laugh at a &quot;dwarf, who wishes to play a giant&quot;. I find the message enthralling, particularly because I myself feel like a dwarf sometimes, wandering about in an &quot;armor&quot; five sizes too big...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4107-littledwarf","user":"LittleDwarf","date":". 10-26-2014, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4107-littledwarf","name":"LittleDwarf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}